-- title:
--   Reading germs at a point in the geometric function field
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial, and the hypothesis $hj$ that $j(q)$ lies in the level-$\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, i.e. a Deligne–Rapoport package for $X_H(M)$ over $R_p$ comprising properness, flatness, integrality, local finite presentation and normality of `X p (ΓM M H) hj`, together with a curve model `Meta` over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with function field $F :=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` and an isomorphism `eeta` of `Meta.C` with the base change of the model to $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit, algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R_p \to A$ compatible with $R_p \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O'$ be a discrete valuation domain with maps $\rho_{O'} : R_p \to O'$, an injective local $\iota_{A'} : O' \to A$ with $\iota_{A'} \circ \rho_{O'} = \rho$, and $j_{O'} : O' \to \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $j_{O'} \circ \rho_{O'}$ the structure map and $j_{O'}$ the composite of $\iota_{A'}$ with $A \hookrightarrow \bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, the induced residue maps agreeing. Let $x'$ be a point of $X_{O'} :=$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO'` lying over the closed point of $O'$, $B$ the stalk there, $\sigma_B : O' \to B$ the structural map, and $\mathrm{prJ}'$ the base-change morphism from $X_{\bar{\mathbb{Q}}}$ to $X_{O'}$ along $j_{O'}$. Assume the image under $\mathrm{prJ}' \circ \mathrm{eeta}$ of the generic point of `Meta.C` specialises to $x'$, and let $\mathrm{emb} : B \to F$ be the resulting composite of specialisation, the stalk maps of $\mathrm{prJ}'$ and $\mathrm{eeta}$, and `Meta.ffEquiv.symm`. Then: $\sigma_B$ is local, $\mathrm{emb}$ is injective and $\mathrm{emb} \circ \sigma_B$ equals $\bar{\mathbb{Q}} \to F$ composed after $j_{O'}$; moreover, for every place $W$ of $F$ over $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field is generated by $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$, and every $s' : \operatorname{Spec} A \to X_{O'}$ over $\operatorname{Spec} \iota_{A'}$ whose restriction along $\operatorname{Spec}(A \hookrightarrow \bar{\mathbb{Q}})$ is the $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$-point corresponding to $W$ under `Meta.pointEquivPlace`, pushed forward by $\mathrm{eeta}$ and $\mathrm{prJ}'$, and with $s'$ sending the closed point of $A$ to $x'$, the induced $\chi : B \to A$ is local, satisfies $\chi \circ \sigma_B = \iota_{A'}$, and for every $b \in B$ one has $\mathrm{emb}(b)$ in the valuation subring of $W$ with $W.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{emb}(b))$ equal to the image of $\chi(b)$ in $\bar{\mathbb{Q}}$.
--
--   This is the point-generic form of the stalk-reading lemma for the Deligne–Rapoport integral model base-changed to a coefficient discrete valuation ring: germs at a point over the closed fibre are read injectively inside the geometric function field, constants are read as constants, and evaluation at a rational place agrees with the residue of the corresponding $A$-section. It is used in the arguments identifying the image of the stalk reading with rings of integral functions, for both the algebraisation at a node and the Hartogs-type extension at a smooth point.
